{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q005_cupredoxin_function_transfer","answer":"In SCOPe 2.08, these are distinct families within the Cupredoxins superfamily b.6.1 (SUNID 49503): Plastocyanin/azurin-like, b.6.1.1 (49504); Ephrin ectodomain, b.6.1.5 (74874); and Peptidylarginine deiminase Pad4, N-terminal domain, b.6.1.6 (110107). They share the Cupredoxin-like fold b.6 (49502), in the All beta proteins class b (48724). Their shared superfamily indicates probable common evolutionary ancestry, a stronger claim than fold similarity alone; it does not imply identical function or membership in the same family.

SCOPe explicitly describes both ephrin ectodomains and the PAD4 N-terminal domain as probably related to cupredoxins but lacking the metal-binding site. Thus, copper binding and electron transfer must not be transferred from canonical plastocyanin/azurin proteins to either family. Ephrins function in receptor-mediated signaling. PAD4 is a calcium-dependent peptidylarginine deiminase, but this classification concerns its N-terminal domain, not its catalytic domain or the entire enzyme.

A shared scaffold may support a structural template for the conserved core, but cannot establish a copper site or redox function. Such assignments require target-specific evidence for conserved copper-coordinating residues and their three-dimensional geometry, metal occupancy or binding measurements, and biochemical evidence of electron transfer. Neither the superfamily name nor family membership alone guarantees these activities.","evidence_used":["Pretrained model knowledge","mcp__scope__search_scop","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","mcp__scope__list_scop_children","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Cupredoxins&mode=auto&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/b.6.1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/b.6.1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/b.6.1/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49504","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/74874","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/74874/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110107","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110107/annotations"]}]}
